\image{conf-mtsinai-scc-dbs-cv.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} \strong{Subcallosal-cingulate (SCC) DBS} for treatment-resistant depression, read out by \strong{computer vision} instead of ordinal clinician scales. From self-recorded at-home video diaries (twice daily, n=12 over 7 months, ~4600 videos), facial-landmark extraction (MediaPipe) + affine decomposition separates rigid head movement from local face motion, quantifying psychomotor retardation — a cardinal TRD sign that traditional scales miss. Motor retardation resolves shortly post-stimulation. The behavioral-readout end of a deep-brain therapy.}
